ts and measurements. Having common measurements would have been useful when people traded goods or worked on construction, especially between different settlements.By around 1900 BCE, many of the larger cities began to decline. There does not seem to have been one clear reason for this change. Climate changes, shifts in river patterns, environmental problems, and changes in trade may have contributed to it. Even so, the people did not simply disappear. Many continued living in smaller settlements, and parts of their culture and traditions survived in communities that came later.
