ion easier, especially when goods were exchanged between different settlements.By around 1900 BCE, many of the larger cities started to decline. There was probably not just one reason for this. Changes in climate, changes in river patterns, environmental issues and a reduction in trade may have all played a part. Even though the large cities declined, the people themselves did not suddenly disappear. Many continued living in smaller settlements, and some of their traditions and ways of life continued among later communities.
