nd measurements. A common system would have helped people when trading goods and doing construction work, especially across different settlements.Around 1900 BCE, many of the larger cities began to decline. There is no single explanation for why this happened. Changes in climate and river patterns, environmental problems and changes in trade may all have contributed. Still, the decline of the cities did not mean that the people completely disappeared. Many moved to or continued living in smaller settlements, and parts of their traditions and culture carried on in later communities.
